from langchain_experimental.text_splitter import SemanticChunker
from langchain_huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbeddings

embeddings = HuggingFaceEmbeddings(
    model_name="sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2"
)
text = """
The human brain is one of the most complex organs in the human body. It controls thoughts, emotions, memory, movement, and decision-making through billions of interconnected neurons. These neurons communicate using electrical and chemical signals, allowing the brain to process information from the surrounding environment. Scientists continue to study how memories are formed, how people learn new skills, and how sleep influences cognitive performance. Regular exercise, sufficient sleep, balanced nutrition, and continuous learning can support overall brain health.
The history of space exploration represents humanity's desire to understand the universe beyond Earth. Early astronomers observed planets and stars using simple instruments, while modern scientists use powerful telescopes, satellites, and robotic spacecraft to investigate distant celestial objects. Space missions have discovered evidence of water on Mars, examined the atmospheres of distant planets, and improved our understanding of black holes and galaxies. Engineers are also developing reusable rockets to reduce launch costs and make space travel more accessible. Future missions may establish permanent research stations on the Moon and investigate the possibility of human exploration of Mars.
Photography is an art that combines creativity with technical knowledge. A photographer must understand lighting, composition, perspective, and camera settings to capture meaningful images. Aperture controls the amount of light entering the camera and influences background blur, while shutter speed determines how long the sensor receives light. ISO sensitivity affects how the camera responds to available light. Natural lighting can create soft and realistic images, whereas artificial lighting allows photographers to control shadows and highlights. Beyond technical settings, storytelling and the ability to recognize interesting moments often distinguish an ordinary photograph from a memorable one.
The ocean contains an enormous variety of living organisms, many of which remain unknown to scientists. Coral reefs support diverse marine ecosystems, providing shelter and food for fish, mollusks, crustaceans, and countless other species. Deep-sea environments contain organisms adapted to extreme pressure, low temperatures, and complete darkness. However, marine ecosystems face serious threats from plastic pollution, rising ocean temperatures, overfishing, and habitat destruction. Protecting these environments requires international cooperation, responsible fishing practices, scientific research, and effective conservation policies.
Cooking traditions reflect the history, geography, and cultural identity of different communities. Ingredients available in a particular region strongly influence its traditional dishes, while migration and trade introduce new flavors and techniques. Fermentation, roasting, steaming, and slow cooking produce different textures and flavors through physical and chemical changes. Understanding ingredient proportions and cooking temperatures helps improve consistency and food safety. Modern chefs frequently combine traditional recipes with contemporary methods, creating new dishes while preserving important culinary traditions.
Learning a programming language requires more than memorizing syntax. Beginners must understand variables, data types, conditional statements, loops, functions, and data structures before building complex applications. Regular practice helps learners recognize patterns and develop problem-solving abilities. Small projects provide opportunities to apply theoretical knowledge, identify mistakes, and improve debugging skills. As programmers gain experience, they begin to explore software architecture, testing, version control, databases, and deployment. Consistent practice and reviewing previous mistakes are essential for long-term improvement.
Climate change is affecting ecosystems, agriculture, coastal communities, and weather patterns across the world. Rising global temperatures contribute to melting glaciers, increasing sea levels, and changing rainfall distribution. These changes can create challenges for farmers, particularly in regions that depend heavily on seasonal rainfall. Renewable energy technologies, including solar and wind power, can reduce dependence on fossil fuels. Improving energy efficiency, protecting forests, developing sustainable transportation, and reducing waste are additional measures that can help address environmental challenges.
Human relationships depend on communication, trust, empathy, and mutual respect. Listening carefully allows people to understand perspectives that differ from their own, while clear communication reduces unnecessary misunderstandings. Emotional intelligence helps individuals recognize their feelings and respond thoughtfully during difficult conversations. Healthy relationships also require boundaries, honesty, and the willingness to resolve disagreements constructively. Although conflicts are a normal part of human interaction, respectful communication can help people maintain stronger personal and professional connections.
Modern cities face increasing challenges related to transportation, housing, pollution, and energy consumption. Urban planners design roads, public transportation networks, parks, residential neighborhoods, and commercial districts to support growing populations. Efficient public transport can reduce traffic congestion and lower emissions, while green spaces improve environmental quality and provide places for recreation. Smart infrastructure can use sensors and data analysis to monitor traffic, manage electricity consumption, and improve public services. Successful urban development requires balancing economic growth, environmental protection, accessibility, and the needs of local communities.
Scientific research advances knowledge through observation, experimentation, measurement, and critical analysis. Researchers develop hypotheses, collect evidence, and compare their findings with existing explanations. Experiments must be designed carefully to reduce bias and produce reliable results. Other scientists evaluate published research, attempt to reproduce important findings, and identify limitations in the methods used. Scientific conclusions may change when stronger evidence becomes available. This process of continuous testing and revision allows scientific knowledge to develop over time.
"""



text_splitter = SemanticChunker(
    embeddings=embeddings,
    breakpoint_threshold_type="standard_deviation",
    breakpoint_threshold_amount=3
)

docs=text_splitter.create_documents([text])
# print(docs)


for i in range(len(docs)):
    print(f"\n--- Chunk {i+1} ---")
    print(docs[i].page_content)